2d game

testing commit

## Running
- python main.py            the full game: walk the path (A / D), walk into an enemy to fight it
- python combat_proto.py    one test fight against the Lantern Stag
- python combat_proto.py maw   (or moth / stag / pilgrim / bellwether) to test another enemy
Asset paths are relative to this folder, so these work from any directory.

## Files
- main.py          overworld: walking, camera, enemies on the path, starts fights, permadeath
- combat_proto.py  the typing combat. main.py calls run_combat(enemy_key, player_hp)
- enemies.py       one table with every enemy (spritesheet frames, HP, attack, flavour text)
- sprites.py       image helpers shared by both (cut frames, align by feet, outline, ...)
- scene.py         forest parallax background
- tools/measure_frames.py   re-measures an enemy sheet's frame rectangles (needs numpy + pillow)

## Starting a fight
Walking into an enemy plays a short encounter (about 1.5 s: "!", the enemy rears up, the screen
closes to black), then combat opens with an intro (about 2.6 s: fade in, both fighters step in,
the enemy's name, "Ready... CAST!"). Nothing you type counts until "CAST!", so keys held or
pressed while walking can't end up in the spell box. The win/lose box also ignores keys for 1 s.
Timings: ENCOUNTER_FRAMES in main.py, INTRO_TIME and friends at the top of combat_proto.py.

## Combat controls
- Type a spell's incantation, then Enter to cast it
- Tab / Shift+Tab, Up / Down, or 1-6: switch the selected spell
- Typing the start of another spell's incantation switches to that spell automatically
- A misspelled incantation fizzles and the enemy gets a free turn
- Standalone test fight: R fights again after a win/loss. From main.py: Enter continues
- Esc: quit

## Critical hits (typing speed)
Speed is measured in words per minute (1 word = 5 letters), from the first letter typed until Enter.
- 121+ WPM: 50%   101-120: 33%   81-100: 25%   61-80: 15%   60 or less: 5%
A crit does 1.5x damage (CRIT_MULTIPLIER). Ward and Mend can't crit. The table is CRIT_TABLE
at the top of combat_proto.py. The input box shows your live WPM and crit chance while typing.

## Adding things
- A spell: write an effect function (see spark_effect), then add a Spell(...) to the grimoire list.
- An enemy: add an entry to ENEMIES in enemies.py, then put it on the path in ENEMY_PLACEMENTS in main.py.

Layout knobs (top of combat_proto.py): GROUND_Y, PLAYER_FEET, ENEMY_X,
SCENE_PATH_Y (where the dirt path is in the scene art; the scene is shifted so it lines up with GROUND_Y).
